================================================================================

The corpora under data/ are DERIVED WORKS of the Natural Questions dataset
(Kwiatkowski et al., 2019), whose documents are Wikipedia articles. Wikipedia
text is licensed CC BY-SA 3.0, and Natural Questions is distributed under the
same terms. Because CC BY-SA is a "share-alike" (copyleft) licence, these
derived files must remain under CC BY-SA 3.0 and CANNOT be relicensed under the
MIT licence that covers this repository's source code.

You are free to share and adapt these files, provided you:
  - ATTRIBUTE the source (Natural Questions + Wikipedia) — see ../SOURCES.md;
  - license any redistributed derivative under CC BY-SA 3.0 (SHARE-ALIKE).

Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

The code that produced these files (src/, scripts/) is separately MIT-licensed;
see ../LICENSE. This CC BY-SA notice governs the DATA CONTENT only, not the
extraction code.
